// Sections match URANUS_SCROLL_PATH waypoints in PlanetScrollCameras.ts.

const items = [
  {
    id:       'triforge-gui',
    category: 'CONCEPT',
    title:    'Triforge Stage 2: A GUI Node Editor',
    meta:     'Roadmap · Not started',
    body: [
      'Triforge\'s 19 packages are all code-first — you wire up node graphs in TypeScript, the same way you\'d script Blender rather than click through its editor. Stage 2 is the obvious next step: an actual visual node-editor application, so a graph can be built and previewed without writing the equivalent JavaScript by hand.',
      'The hard part isn\'t the canvas — it\'s making the visual graph and the code-first API stay in sync, so a graph built in the editor exports to the exact same TypeScript a developer would have written directly. Neither direction should be a second-class citizen.',
      'This is roadmap, not shipped — it is listed publicly specifically so the gap between "19 packages, code-first" and "a real visual tool" stays honest rather than implied to already exist.',
    ],
    topics: ['Why It\'s Needed', 'The Hard Part', 'Current Status'],
  },
  {
    id:       'triforge-terrain',
    category: 'CONCEPT',
    title:    'Terrain & Vegetation Addon Suite',
    meta:     'Roadmap · Not started',
    body: [
      'Triforge\'s existing packages cover geometry, shading, particles, physics, and animation — but nothing purpose-built for the specific case of procedural terrain and vegetation scattering, the kind of thing Blender\'s own geometry-nodes ecosystem leans on heavily.',
      'The plan is an addon suite on top of the existing `geometry-nodes` and `modifier-core` packages rather than a ground-up rewrite — terrain heightfields, erosion-style noise, and instanced vegetation scatter that respects slope and altitude, compiled the same way every other Triforge graph is.',
      'Nothing here is built yet. It is next on the public roadmap after the Stage 2 GUI, not a parallel effort — sequencing matters more than scope here.',
    ],
    topics: ['The Gap', 'The Plan', 'Sequencing'],
  },
  {
    id:       'ai-dev-kit-self-improvement',
    category: 'CONCEPT',
    title:    'Self-Improving Skills, Taken Further',
    meta:     'ai-dev-kit · Existing feature, open direction',
    body: [
      'ai-dev-kit already keeps a gitignored `learnings.md` per project, so lessons an agent picks up stay local to that codebase instead of leaking upstream. The open question is how far that self-improvement loop can go without turning into noise.',
      'Right now a skill loads on trigger and stays static within a session — the interesting next step is whether a skill could propose a small, reviewable edit to its own instructions based on a pattern of repeated corrections, with a human still approving the change before it lands.',
      'This is a direction being actively thought through on the real repo, not a shipped feature — the current, working version of the kit is already public and usable without it.',
    ],
    topics: ['What Exists Today', 'The Open Question', 'What\'s Already Real'],
  },
  {
    id:       'laya-ai-system-2',
    category: 'CONCEPT',
    title:    'System 2 Reasoning for Laya-AI',
    meta:     'Fish Pond · Known limitation, not implemented',
    body: [
      'Fish Pond\'s Underwater scene already runs Laya-AI, an on-device ONNX model, for fast, reflex-style fish decisions. What it explicitly does not have yet is slower, deliberative reasoning — a "System 2" layer that could weigh competing goals instead of reacting to the nearest stimulus.',
      'Laya-AI today is a general text classifier repurposed for this task, not a fish-specific model — the README names this as a known limitation, not a hidden one. Adding real deliberative behaviour would mean a second, slower model (or a rules layer) sitting on top of the existing reflex model, not replacing it.',
      'Listed here as what Fish Pond\'s own documentation already flags as unfinished, not as a new idea invented for this page.',
    ],
    topics: ['What Runs Today', 'The Missing Layer', 'Documented, Not Hidden'],
  },
];
